      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. This is motivated by https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/532256, right? It doesn\u0027t seem like it really protects us any more than what we had? Could we at least store the sizeof T in the GrSubRunAllocator (only in debug builds?), and then assert that it matches sizeof(*this) in the Slug and TextBlob constructors? Or (even better) - can we template GrSubRunAllocator on T, so that it\u0027s compile-time impossible to pass the wrong \"type\" of allocator to the containing class?",
